MIDI out of a plugin processed in pieces keeps its time (Segno: docs/design/midi-effects.md §15).

A plugin whose parameters move is processed in pieces of 128 samples (fine-grain automation),
each piece's MIDI timed from the piece's start. The first piece's output became the block's as
it was (its start is the block's); later pieces' output was merged without moving it back to
the block's time, so a note a plugin passed on or played in a later piece came out early, by
the piece's offset. Each piece's MIDI now goes back to the block's time before it's merged.

